.TH "PB-CONFIG-SYNC-PATH" "1" "Sep 2026" "Paperboat" "Paperboat CLI"

.SH NAME
pb-config-sync-path - Show the authoritative machine configuration path


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBpb config sync path [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Show the authoritative machine configuration path

.PP
Print the authoritative local machine configuration path so you can edit or inspect the source file. This command only resolves the location; it does not create a file or change the machine's synchronization assignment.

.PP
Configuration commands distinguish local CLI settings from synchronized repository content. Inspect current state before changing it; synchronization reports conflicts instead of silently overwriting one side. The --json option provides structured output for scripts where supported.

.PP
JSON output is supported with --json.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for path

.PP
\fB--json\fP[=false]
	print the authoritative path as JSON


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--config\fP=""
	path to the CLI config file

.PP
\fB--no-customization\fP[=false]
	ignore local shortcuts, command defaults, and TUI preferences

.PP
\fB--server\fP=""
	paperboat-server base URL override

.PP
\fB--workspace\fP=""
	resource workspace selector: personal or a team slug


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBpb-config-sync(1)\fP
